            0.049,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Another Peek Beyond the Point"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.088,
            0.78,
            0.134
          ],
          "content": "(c) product greater than 150 (d) product nearest to 100 (e) product nearest to 5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.137,
            0.73,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": "11. Sort the following expressions in increasing order: (a) 245.05 × 0.942368 (b) 245.05 × 7.9682 (c) 245.05 ÷ 7.9682 (d) 245.05 ÷ 0.942368 (e) 245.05 (f) 7.9682"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.408,
            0.268,
            0.59,
            0.293
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "SUMMARY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.302,
            0.822,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": "In this chapter, we learnt procedures to perform decimal multiplication and division."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.34,
            0.824,
            0.415
          ],
          "content": "For decimal multiplication, we first multiply the multiplier and multiplicand as counting numbers. The number of decimal digits in the product is the total number of decimal digits in the multiplier and multiplicand."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.416,
            0.823,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": "Division of decimals uses the same procedure, i.e., division using place value (long division), as with counting numbers. The regrouping continues after the Ones place to Tenths, Hundredths, Thousandths, and so on. When the Ones are regrouped to Tenths, a decimal point is placed in the quotient."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.512,
            0.821,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "There are decimal divisions where the quotient never ends. After each regrouping and dividing there is always a remainder!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.431,
            0.593,
            0.573,
            0.615
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "LIT' PUZZLE TIME!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.469,
            0.627,
            0.544,
            0.647
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Hidato"
        },
